            <title>[LU-21141] nodemap: nodemap_clear_dynamic_nodemaps() walks nm_list without the lock</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21141</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;nodemap_clear_dynamic_nodemaps()&lt;/tt&gt; links the nodemaps through &lt;tt&gt;nm_list&lt;/tt&gt; under &lt;tt&gt;active_config_lock&lt;/tt&gt;. It then drops the lock and walks the list. Other code relinks &lt;tt&gt;nm_list&lt;/tt&gt; under that lock, and a concurrent call of the function does the same. The walk then follows a list that it does not own.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;mgs_iocontrol_nodemap()&lt;/tt&gt; calls this function after a nodemap change when dynamic nodemaps exist and the MGS has a local target. Thus two concurrent nodemap commands on such an MGS can crash or hang the node. &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19478" title="dynamic nodemaps are not removed when persistent nodemaps are changed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19478"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19478&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; added the function, so all branches with that change have the defect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Reproduction"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Reproduction&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On a VM, I added a delay between the unlock and the walk. One nodemap change waited at the delay, and a second change then ran. The node crashed as soon as the delay ended:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address 0000ffff9906144c
Internal error: Oops: 0000000096000006 [#1] SMP
pc : nodemap_clear_dynamic_nodemaps+0x12c/0x230 [ptlrpc]
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The delay widens the window. I did not reproduce the crash without the delay.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Fix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Fix&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Copy the dynamic nodemap names under &lt;tt&gt;active_config_lock&lt;/tt&gt;, and delete by name after the unlock.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Let only one call of the function delete at a time, because &lt;tt&gt;nodemap_del()&lt;/tt&gt; walks &lt;tt&gt;nm_subnodemaps&lt;/tt&gt; without the lock.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Move the &lt;tt&gt;nm_parent_entry&lt;/tt&gt; unlink in &lt;tt&gt;nodemap_destroy()&lt;/tt&gt; under &lt;tt&gt;active_config_lock&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Remaininggaps"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Remaining gaps&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;An explicit &lt;tt&gt;nodemap_del&lt;/tt&gt; that runs with a clear still walks &lt;tt&gt;nm_subnodemaps&lt;/tt&gt; without the lock.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The check that a name is dynamic and the delete are not atomic. If an administrator removes a dynamic nodemap and adds a persistent nodemap with that name in this window, the clear removes the persistent nodemap. The earlier code has the same window.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
